    "turn_idx": 4,
    "turn_text": "but I appreciate you taking the time to talk to us tonight. Thank you for having us on. Oh, it's my pleasure. Now, I was aware of you before because I had heard this statement here or the comment there, and I always thought, now this woman is tough. She's the kind of person we need in Congress. But last weekend, or actually now maybe it was two weeks ago, I got a double dose of Congresswoman Marcy Capture. First, in Michael Moore's movie, you stole the show and you had the people in the theater cheering you. And I know that's happening in theaters across the country. And then the next night, I saw you with Bill Maher on real time. And again, you had me cheering you. Well, thank you for the things you're doing and you're saying. Let's start with one thing that you said with Bill Maher that totally got me. You said we need money disarmament in the Congress. And it was so heartening for me to hear you say that because I had a sort of a revelation that weekend. And it seems to me that the reason we are not getting things done, the reason that we're having this fight over healthcare reform is money. Is there another reason that this is an ongoing battle?",
