    "turn_text": "it too good. Life has been too good for too long. They've lost a sense of the struggle. And it's just a tragedy. In this health bill, for example, one of the provisions that amazes me is the one dealing with the right to negotiate price of pharmaceuticals if you bulk buy. They don't require it. If we're going to save money and try to help people who don't have insurance and try to help people who have insurance not lose it, we know that we need to buy insurance policies. Some of the money for that is currently being wasted on this endless advertising on television and other media for buying pharmaceuticals. Back when I was a kid, there weren't all these ads for pharmaceuticals. You need something. Your doctor tells you what you need to get and you go get it. All this money is being wasted, sort of pushing pharmaceuticals on people. And I think any group of businesses that has that much money to buy up the airwaves for heaven's sake. has got some room in their budget to cut back. And without negotiated pricing for pharmaceuticals, we're not going to save the money we need to pay the health bills.",
